00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:34.030
are facing a revolution
in customer care.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:36.490
33% of retail
customers will consider

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.400
switching to a
different retailer,

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.980
if they've had a bad experience.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:45.800
And estimates show that
over the next several years,

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.120
AI will be a large component
of providing service

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.540
to customers in call centers.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.290
So it's important to
be thinking about how

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.810
you can leverage
artificial intelligence

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:00.030
and make impact
in your business.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.490
Google Cloud's context
center AI solution

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.680
is built for this
new world, based

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.610
around conversational core that
understands human interaction

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.010
and incorporates the context.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.170
At its core, this
virtual agent AI

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.930
handles incoming
calls or messages

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.480
and engages in natural
human-like dialogue

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:22.380
to handle common use
cases and flows, including

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.420
having to go off script.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.700
When the call can't be
handled automatically,

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.680
it's passed to a human agent.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.770
And the Agent Assist
AI steps into support

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.160
with the relevant content from
the knowledge base and context

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.080
about the user and
their situation.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:42.180
The insights AI then
surfaces trends and analysis

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:45.540
to help the entire
system improve.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:47.910
For retailers, the fact
that it's centralized

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.280
means you can apply
consistent intelligence

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.250
across every application
in the customer journey.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.980
The biggest cost
savings can often

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:59.875
be found from deflecting voice
calls into your contact center.

00:14:59.875 --> 00:15:01.500
But there's been
challenges in the past

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.780
because conversations
can meander

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:07.470
and [? IVR ?] trees may
not be able to adapt.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.710
The inability to flex to
human conversation style

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.200
has also historically
limited the ability

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.870
to assist agents in real time.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.140
Contact Center AI has the
ability to go off script,

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:22.470
so you can work outside
the predefined flow,

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:26.250
answering complex questions,
full of unexpected stops

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:29.980
and starts, word choices,
or implied meanings.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:32.400
Contact Center AI
also has the ability

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:36.120
to handle multiple use
cases for your customers,

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.540
like taking a payment, updating
information, like a phone

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:44.010
number, giving them information
about store hours, which then

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:46.530
allows you to fully
automate routine tasks

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.020
and further deflect calls.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.910
You can start with
an easy use case

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:55.020
and grow your adoption depending
on your organization's needs.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.780
During COVID-19, for
example, many retailers

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:00.450
were faced with a deluge
of customer inquiries

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:03.960
specific to store timing
and special hours.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.020
Our team offered up a rapid
response virtual agent

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.200
that could be set up in days
and take the volume of calls

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.290
off your busy agents, and
most importantly, make sure

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:16.080
that customers felt
supported through this period

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.390
of heightened anxiety.

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.460
Marks &amp; Spencer is
one of the customers

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.490
we worked with in the
contact center space.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:27.630
They work with our Partner
Develop to leverage Dialogflow

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:31.650
to help manage their
contact center interactions.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.380
Marks &amp; Spencer is one of the
best beloved retail brands

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.860
in the UK with over 30
million loyal customers.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:41.280
And they had switchboards in
13 different store locations

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.270
across their store footprint.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:46.080
And they were taking nine
million calls a year.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.020
You can imagine that's a lot to
understand the different things

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.910
that customers may
be calling about,

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:54.570
specific to that store, but
also broader questions that can

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.700
be answered more effectively.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:00.300
Using Dialogflow, they were
able to reduce that call volume

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:05.460
to the stores by 50% and route
more than 7 million calls

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:08.050
